+# Boundary inspection: Membership Administrator role
+
+This note captures the existing aggregate, projection, onboarding conversion, and
+test-support boundaries inspected for task 001 of the iteration plan. It is
+intended to guide the later role/permission design without changing behaviour.
+
+## Binding architecture constraints
+
+- ADR 0002 says new domain behaviour should use Commanded commands,
+  aggregates, events, and read-model projections by default.
+- ADR 0007 keeps club, person, and membership lifecycle behaviour inside the
+  Membership Commanded context (`Memba.Membership.App` and
+  `Memba.Membership.Router`). Other contexts should depend on Membership's
+  public query API rather than its projection tables.
+- ADR 0008 uses the persistent PostgreSQL EventStore adapter in development and
+  test, so new role/permission events need EventStore-backed tests rather than
+  an in-memory shortcut.
+- ADR 0009 uses `commanded_ecto_projections`; role/permission read models should
+  follow the existing projector pattern rather than custom event handlers.
+- ADR 0011 uses caller-generated UUID aggregate identities. Any new role,
+  assignment, or permission-grant aggregate identities should be supplied by the
+  application service/test before dispatch.
+- ADR 0022 uses projection barriers/read-your-writes synchronization. Acceptance
+  steps that assert role/permission projection state should use existing
+  strong-consistency dispatches or projection barriers.
+
+## Current Membership write-side boundaries
+
+Membership has one Commanded application and router:
+
+- `Memba.Membership.App` is the Commanded application.
+- `Memba.Membership.Router` identifies three aggregate roots:
+  - `Memba.Membership.Club`, routed by `:club_id`;
+  - `Memba.Membership.Person`, routed by `:person_id`;
+  - `Memba.Membership.Membership`, routed by `:membership_id`.
+
+Current commands and events are intentionally narrow:
+
+- Club creation/update:
+  - commands: `CreateClub`, `UpdateClub`;
+  - events: `ClubCreated`, `ClubUpdated`;
+  - aggregate state: `club_id`, `name`, `slug`.
+- Person creation/email replacement:
+  - commands: `CreatePerson`, `ReplacePersonEmailAddresses`;
+  - events: `PersonCreated`, `PersonEmailAddressesReplaced`;
+  - aggregate state: `person_id`, name, legacy primary email, and email set.
+- Membership add/remove:
+  - commands: `AddMember`, `RemoveMember`;
+  - events: `MemberAdded`, `MemberRemoved`;
+  - aggregate state: `membership_id`, `club_id`, `person_id`, `active`.
+
+Duplicate active memberships for a `{club_id, person_id}` pair are enforced in
+the public `Memba.Membership.add_member/2` application service by querying the
+membership projection before dispatch. The `Membership` aggregate only protects
+its own `membership_id` stream. Slug and email uniqueness are enforced in the
+same public API layer before dispatch.
+
+## Current Membership read-side boundaries
+
+Existing projected tables/schemas:
+
+- `membership_clubs` / `Memba.Membership.Projections.Club`;
+- `membership_people` / `Memba.Membership.Projections.Person`;
+- `membership_person_email_addresses` /
+  `Memba.Membership.Projections.PersonEmailAddress`;
+- `membership_memberships` / `Memba.Membership.Projections.Membership`.
+
+Existing projectors:
+
+- `Memba.Membership.Projectors.Club` projects `ClubCreated` and `ClubUpdated`;
+- `Memba.Membership.Projectors.Person` projects `PersonCreated` and
+  `PersonEmailAddressesReplaced`;
+- `Memba.Membership.Projectors.Membership` projects `MemberAdded` and
+  `MemberRemoved`.
+
+All Membership projectors use `Commanded.Projections.Ecto` with
+`consistency: :strong` and publish read-model changes through
+`Memba.ReadModelChanges`. New role/permission projectors should be added to:
+
+- the application supervisor;
+- `:event_sourced_projection_tables` config;
+- `Memba.EventSourcedCase` projector/table reset lists;
+- `MembaWeb.DevTestSupportController` acceptance reset/projector lists.
+
+## Onboarding conversion boundary
+
+`Memba.Onboarding` is not event-sourced. It owns the Ecto-backed onboarding
+request record and orchestrates Membership commands during conversion:
+
+1. lock/fetch an active `onboarding_requests` row;
+2. generate `club_id` and `membership_id`;
+3. choose a requester `person_id`, reusing an existing Membership person by
+   normalized requester email when possible;
+4. dispatch `Membership.create_club/2` with `consistency: :strong`;
+5. dispatch `Membership.create_person/2` only when the requester person is new;
+6. dispatch `Membership.add_member/2` with `consistency: :strong`;
+7. mark the onboarding request converted with the generated IDs;
+8. load projected club/person read models;
+9. deliver the welcome email after conversion is persisted.
+
+The approved requester/first-member role assignment should therefore happen
+after club and membership creation have succeeded, and before returning a
+successful conversion if callers need read-your-writes behaviour. The conversion
+path already has a clear place to add a follow-up Membership role-assignment
+command with strong consistency.
+
+## Staff/admin and member-management entry points
+
+Current staff-only screens call the Membership public API directly:
+
+- staff club creation: `MembaWeb.Admin.ClubsLive.Index`;
+- staff club update/member add/member remove:
+  `MembaWeb.Admin.ClubsLive.Show`;
+- staff person creation: `MembaWeb.Admin.PeopleLive.New`.
+
+These are platform/staff operations today. Later authorization work should keep
+staff access separate from club-scoped Membership Administrator permission
+checks, as required by the plan.
+
+Current member-facing flows use Membership projections for access and recipient
+resolution:
+
+- member sign-in/club list queries active memberships by email;
+- club site routing checks `Membership.active_member_of_club_by_email?/2`;
+- Messaging resolves recipients through `Membership.list_active_members_of_club/1`
+  per ADR 0007.
+
+## Test-support and seed creation paths
+
+Automated test and acceptance setup currently creates club/person/membership
+state through a mix of public API, raw command dispatch, and direct projection
+inserts:
+
+- Cucumber Membership steps use direct `Memba.Membership.App.dispatch/2` for
+  some `CreateClub`, `CreatePerson`, and `AddMember` setup.
+- Request-account/authentication Cucumber steps use the public
+  `Memba.Membership` API.
+- `Memba.MembershipFixtures` inserts projection rows directly for projection and
+  query tests.
+- `priv/repo/seeds.exs` inserts representative projection rows directly.
+- Controller/LiveView/unit tests mostly use the public Membership API, with some
+  lower-level aggregate/dispatch tests intentionally exercising commands/events.
+
+Later tasks that introduce default roles and flattened permission projections
+will need to update both event-sourced setup paths and direct-projection setup
+paths so tests, seeds, and acceptance resets have coherent role/permission read
+models.
